  "description": "JAWPUV crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C112 H100 Cl4 Gd7 N8 O36 Zn4 1+,4(C2 H3 N1),Cl1 1-,4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn3 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn4 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.327-4.340 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.93-132.22°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Zn4Gd7(L)8(O2)2(OH)4(Cl)4(H2O)4]·Cl·4H2O·4CH3CN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
